<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Varying Input Lookbacks</h3>

<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L_{input}&lt;512}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐋</mi><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐩𝐮𝐭</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>𝟓𝟏𝟐</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L_{input}&lt;512}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although Super-Linear is a linear forecaster, it includes a simple built-in heuristic to handle variable lookback lengths. When the input lookback <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{input}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{input}}</annotation></semantics></math> is shorter than the training length (<math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{train}}=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{train}}=512</annotation></semantics></math>), the series is upsampled via linear interpolation to match 512. After inference, the output is downsampled back to the original resolution. This process implicitly modifies the signal’s frequency, but Super-Linear remains effective due to its robustness to frequency variations. The resampling factor is computed as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{resample factor}=\left\lceil\frac{L_{train}}{L_{input}}\right\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>resample factor</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{resample factor}=\left\lceil\frac{L_{train}}{L_{input}}\right\rceil</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To revert the output, we interpolate with a factor of <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\text{resample factor}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mtext>resample factor</mtext></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\text{resample factor}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This approach enables Super-Linear to effectively handle a range of input lengths. Examples below illustrate forecasting with lookbacks of 384, 256, and 128 on the Electricity and Weather datasets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15105v1/prediction_lookbacks_ecl.svg" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/309;" width="476" height="309"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Super-Linear forecasting illustration with varying input lookbacks for the Electricity dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15105v1/prediction_lookbacks_weather.svg" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/309;" width="476" height="309"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Super-Linear forecasting illustration with varying input lookbacks for the Weather dataset.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{L_{input}&gt;512}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐋</mi><mi>𝐢𝐧𝐩𝐮𝐭</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>𝟓𝟏𝟐</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{L_{input}&gt;512}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The long lookback resample search algorithm adaptively downsamples time series by evaluating a set of candidate scales (default: <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2,4,6]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2,4,6]</annotation></semantics></math>). For each sequence, it computes the power spectral density (PSD) to estimate signal energy, uses the expert distribution of Super-Linear to assess selection uncertainty, and applies linear interpolation for resampling. The objective is to minimize both energy loss and distributional entropy. To this end, we define a scoring function <math id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="score=entropy+\lambda\cdot penalty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">score=entropy+\lambda\cdot penalty</annotation></semantics></math>, and select the resampling scale with the lowest score. A detailed description of the algorithm is provided in <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 𝐋_𝐢𝐧𝐩𝐮𝐭&gt;𝟓𝟏𝟐. ‣ A.7 Varying Input Lookbacks ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Experiments and Results ‣ Super-Linear: A Lightweight Pretrained Mixture of Linear Experts for Time Series Forecasting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Here is an overview of the flow of the algorithm:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lines 1-3</span>, Compute the noramlized periodogram <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{norm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{norm}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the maximal scale factor <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{max}</annotation></semantics></math> allowed such that the energy loss will not surpass <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{max\ loss}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.410em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{max\ loss}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lines 4-10</span>, create a dictionary <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{penalty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{penalty}</annotation></semantics></math> that saves the estimated energy loss incured by each scale parameter <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\in S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lines 13-23</span>, Search for the best sacle parameter that ensures minimal enrtopy score energy loss with the term <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="score=entropy(G(X_{interp}))\ +\lambda A_{penalty}[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">score=entropy(G(X_{interp}))\ +\lambda A_{penalty}[s]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Line 24</span> Finally, return the interpolated input <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{output}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{output}</annotation></semantics></math> and the corresponding scale factor <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{output}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{output}</annotation></semantics></math>, which will be used for resampling the output from Super-Linear to the original granularity.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the algorithm handles long-context inputs containing low-frequency components that may fall outside the range of Super-Linear’s frequency experts. It selects an appropriate resampling factor that shifts the input frequencies into a space the model can represent, while preserving the signal’s energy to avoid information loss.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Long Lookback Resample Search Algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, scales <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{s_{1},s_{2},\ldots\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{s_{1},s_{2},\ldots\}</annotation></semantics></math>, energy loss penalty scaler <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, a pre-trained Super-Linear model, and a parameter <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\max\ \text{loss}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.577em">⁡</mo><mtext>loss</mtext></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\max\ \text{loss}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the maximal energy loss constraint.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\text{norm}}\leftarrow\tfrac{I(X-\bar{X})}{\|I(X-\bar{X})\|_{1}}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>norm</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\text{norm}}\leftarrow\tfrac{I(X-\bar{X})}{\|I(X-\bar{X})\|_{1}}\in\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>  (Periodogram normalization)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{*}\leftarrow\max\{j\mid E_{j}\leq 1-E_{\max\ \text{loss}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.577em">⁡</mo><mtext>loss</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{*}\leftarrow\max\{j\mid E_{j}\leq 1-E_{\max\ \text{loss}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>  where <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{j}=\sum_{1}^{j}I_{\text{norm}}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>j</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mtext>norm</mtext><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{j}=\sum_{1}^{j}I_{\text{norm}}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{M}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{M}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\max}\leftarrow\lfloor\tfrac{\omega_{j^{*}}}{\omega_{\min}}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ω</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\max}\leftarrow\lfloor\tfrac{\omega_{j^{*}}}{\omega_{\min}}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>  (<math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> marks the highest frequency experts)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{penalty}}\leftarrow\{\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>penalty</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{penalty}}\leftarrow\{\}</annotation></semantics></math>  (dictionary to track energy loss of each scale <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S,s&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S,s&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\text{Nyq}}\leftarrow\tfrac{0.5}{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext>Nyq</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mn>0.5</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\text{Nyq}}\leftarrow\tfrac{0.5}{s}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{s}\leftarrow\{I_{\text{norm}}^{j}\mid\omega_{j}&gt;\omega_{\text{Nyq}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mtext>norm</mtext><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext>Nyq</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{s}\leftarrow\{I_{\text{norm}}^{j}\mid\omega_{j}&gt;\omega_{\text{Nyq}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\text{lost}}\leftarrow\|I_{s}\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>lost</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\text{lost}}\leftarrow\|I_{s}\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\text{penalty}}[s]\leftarrow\tfrac{E_{\text{lost}}}{E_{\text{total}}+\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>penalty</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>lost</mtext></msub><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\text{penalty}}[s]\leftarrow\tfrac{E_{\text{lost}}}{E_{\text{total}}+\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>  where <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\approx 10^{-10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≈</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\approx 10^{-10}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{output}}\leftarrow X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{output}}\leftarrow X</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{output}}\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{output}}\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="score_{\text{best}}\leftarrow entropy(G(X))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>best</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">score_{\text{best}}\leftarrow entropy(G(X))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S,s&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S,s&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{interp}}\leftarrow interpolate(X,\tfrac{1}{s})\in\mathbb{R}^{L_{\text{interp}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>interp</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>interp</mtext></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{interp}}\leftarrow interpolate(X,\tfrac{1}{s})\in\mathbb{R}^{L_{\text{interp}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{train}}\leq L_{\text{interp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>interp</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{train}}\leq L_{\text{interp}}</annotation></semantics></math>  and <math id="alg1.l17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\leq s_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\leq s_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="score\leftarrow entropy(G(X_{\text{interp}}))+\lambda A_{\text{penalty}}[s]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>interp</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mtext>penalty</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">score\leftarrow entropy(G(X_{\text{interp}}))+\lambda A_{\text{penalty}}[s]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="score&lt;score_{\text{best}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mtext>best</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">score&lt;score_{\text{best}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
                
                
                  <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{output}}\leftarrow s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{output}}\leftarrow s</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
                
                
                  <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{output}}\leftarrow X_{\text{interp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>interp</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{output}}\leftarrow X_{\text{interp}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
                
                
                 <span id="alg1.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l23.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l24.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> <math id="alg1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\text{output}}\in\mathbb{R}^{L_{\text{interp}}},\;s_{\text{output}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>interp</mtext></msub></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\text{output}}\in\mathbb{R}^{L_{\text{interp}}},\;s_{\text{output}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
