</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">bias-complexity tradeoff</span> analysis <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shalev-Shwartz &amp; Ben-David, 2014</a>)</cite>, we can decompose the error into the approximation error <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>app</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and estimation error <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>est</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The term <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>app</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the minimum achievable error by the Super-Linear predictor, whereas the term <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>est</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the difference between the approximation error
and the error achieved by the ERM predictor with the given training data.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First by the triangle inequality:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|Y(X)-\hat{Y}(X)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|Y(X)-\hat{Y}(X)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\|Y(X)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{\beta_{i}}F_{i}(X)+\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{\beta_{i}}F_{i}(X)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{G_{i}}F_{i}(X)\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\|Y(X)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{\beta_{i}}F_{i}(X)+\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{\beta_{i}}F_{i}(X)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{G_{i}}F_{i}(X)\right\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\|Y(X)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{\beta_{i}}F_{i}(X)\right\|+\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{N}(\bar{\beta_{i}}-\bar{G_{i}})F_{i}(X)\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\|Y(X)-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{\beta_{i}}F_{i}(X)\right\|+\left\|\sum_{i=1}^{N}(\bar{\beta_{i}}-\bar{G_{i}})F_{i}(X)\right\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}+\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>app</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>est</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}+\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1. (Frequency) Approximation term <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>app</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}:=\{\hat{\omega}_{1},\dots,\hat{\omega}_{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}:=\{\hat{\omega}_{1},\dots,\hat{\omega}_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of
frequencies covered by the experts.
Write the Fourier expansion of the (zero<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>mean) target as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Y(X)=\sum_{m}\widehat{X}_{m}\,e^{2\pi im\cdot/T},\qquad I_{m}=\lvert\widehat{X}_{m}\rvert^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>m</mi></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y(X)=\sum_{m}\widehat{X}_{m}\,e^{2\pi im\cdot/T},\qquad I_{m}=\lvert\widehat{X}_{m}\rvert^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For now, let’s assume that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, share the same periodicity, formally: <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}^{X}=I_{m}^{Y}=I_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}^{X}=I_{m}^{Y}=I_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the following section, we will remove this assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because each <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> reproduces its <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\omega}_{i}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ω</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\omega}_{i}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the residual after projecting onto those frequencies is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert Y(X)-R(X)\rVert_{2}^{2}=\sum_{\omega_{m}\notin\mathcal{S}}I_{m}\;=:E_{\perp}(X)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert Y(X)-R(X)\rVert_{2}^{2}=\sum_{\omega_{m}\notin\mathcal{S}}I_{m}\;=:E_{\perp}(X).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\;\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}\leq\sqrt{E_{\perp}(X)}\;}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>app</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\;\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}\leq\sqrt{E_{\perp}(X)}\;}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">2. Estimation term <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>est</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume each expert output is bounded by the energy of its frequency,
i.e.</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert F_{i}(X)\rVert_{2}\;\leq\;\gamma\,\sqrt{I_{i}},\qquad\text{for some }\gamma&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for some </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert F_{i}(X)\rVert_{2}\;\leq\;\gamma\,\sqrt{I_{i}},\qquad\text{for some }\gamma&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using Cauchy–Schwarz and the fact that
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}(\bar{\beta_{i}}-\bar{G_{i}})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}(\bar{\beta_{i}}-\bar{G_{i}})=0</annotation></semantics></math> (both weight vectors sum to 1):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>est</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigl\lVert\sum_{i}(\bar{\beta_{i}}-\bar{G_{i}})F_{i}(X)\Bigr\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigl\lVert\sum_{i}(\bar{\beta_{i}}-\bar{G_{i}})F_{i}(X)\Bigr\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Bigl(\sum_{i}(\bar{\beta_{i}}-\bar{G_{i}})^{2}\Bigr)^{\!1/2}\Bigl(\sum_{i}\lVert F_{i}(X)\rVert_{2}^{2}\Bigr)^{\!1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Bigl(\sum_{i}(\bar{\beta_{i}}-\bar{G_{i}})^{2}\Bigr)^{\!1/2}\Bigl(\sum_{i}\lVert F_{i}(X)\rVert_{2}^{2}\Bigr)^{\!1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\gamma\,\|\beta-G\|_{2}\Bigl(\sum_{i}I_{i}\Bigr)^{\!1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\gamma\,\|\beta-G\|_{2}\Bigl(\sum_{i}I_{i}\Bigr)^{\!1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma\,\|\beta-G\|_{2}\,\lVert X\rVert_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma\,\|\beta-G\|_{2}\,\lVert X\rVert_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{2}\leq\|\cdot\|_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{2}\leq\|\cdot\|_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> on probability simplices,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\;\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}\;\leq\;\gamma\,\lVert X\rVert_{2}\,\|\beta-G\|_{1}\;}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>est</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\;\mathcal{E}_{\text{est}}\;\leq\;\gamma\,\lVert X\rVert_{2}\,\|\beta-G\|_{1}\;}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">3. Combined bound.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Putting the two pieces together,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\;\|Y(X)-\hat{Y}(X)\|\;\leq\;\sqrt{E_{\perp}(X)}\;+\;\gamma\,\lVert X\rVert_{2}\,\|\beta-G\|_{1}\;}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></menclose><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\;\|Y(X)-\hat{Y}(X)\|\;\leq\;\sqrt{E_{\perp}(X)}\;+\;\gamma\,\lVert X\rVert_{2}\,\|\beta-G\|_{1}\;}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remarks.</span></p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\perp}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\perp}(X)</annotation></semantics></math> bounds the <em id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">(frequency)<span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>approximation error</em>: the signal
energy outside the span of the <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> expert frequencies.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The second term penalises how far the learned gating
<math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(X)</annotation></semantics></math> is from the optimal <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.
If training makes <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\beta-G\|_{1}\!\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\beta-G\|_{1}\!\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
the total error collapses to the intrinsic
residual <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{E_{\perp}(X)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{E_{\perp}(X)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To incorporate a stricter assumption on the shared periodicity. Specifically, we’ll define <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> as a frequency-dependent factor representing the relative difference in power at frequency <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. To model a measurable difference, we assume <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is small, i.e., <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\delta_{m}|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\delta_{m}|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall m</annotation></semantics></math> for some small <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> can be positive or negative (indicating amplification or attenuation of power at specific frequencies). For simplicity, we can bound the difference across all frequencies.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{m}^{Y}=(1+\delta_{m})I_{m}^{X},\qquad\sum_{\omega_{m}\notin\mathcal{S}}I_{m}^{X}:=E_{\perp}^{X}(X),\qquad\sum_{\omega_{m}\notin\mathcal{S}}I_{m}^{Y}:=E_{\perp}(X)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{m}^{Y}=(1+\delta_{m})I_{m}^{X},\qquad\sum_{\omega_{m}\notin\mathcal{S}}I_{m}^{X}:=E_{\perp}^{X}(X),\qquad\sum_{\omega_{m}\notin\mathcal{S}}I_{m}^{Y}:=E_{\perp}(X)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To bound this, we use the fact that
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\delta_{m}|\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\delta_{m}|\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\delta_{m})I_{m}^{X}\leq(1+\epsilon)I_{m}^{X}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\delta_{m})I_{m}^{X}\leq(1+\epsilon)I_{m}^{X}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}\leq\sqrt{E_{\perp}}\leq\sqrt{1+\epsilon}\sqrt{E_{\perp}^{X}(X)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>app</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mo>⟂</mo><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{app}}\leq\sqrt{E_{\perp}}\leq\sqrt{1+\epsilon}\sqrt{E_{\perp}^{X}(X)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Datasets</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Pre-training Datasets</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we pre-train Super-Linear using a subset of datasets from the Monash Time Series Repository <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Godahewa et al., 2021</a>)</cite> and the PEMS dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, as part of the two-stage training process shown in Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Gating Function. ‣ 3 Super-Linear Mixture-of-Experts ‣ Super-Linear: A Lightweight Pretrained Mixture of Linear Experts for Time Series Forecasting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Specifically, we select datasets with a minimum sequence length of 5,000 timesteps to enable sufficient downsampling. For upsampling, we cap the maximum resampling factor at <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{max}}=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{max}}=20</annotation></semantics></math>, which controls how much a short sequence can be stretched. For example, a sequence of length 40, when upsampled with a factor of 20, results in a sequence of length 800. The pretraining datasets are detailed in Table. <a href="#A3.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ C.1 Pre-training Datasets ‣ Appendix C Datasets ‣ Super-Linear: A Lightweight Pretrained Mixture of Linear Experts for Time Series Forecasting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Datasets used for pre-training.</figcaption>
